# Navigation and Routing

Purpose: single navigation package and centralized route configuration.

## Mandatory rules

- Use `go_router` only; definitions under `lib/app/router/`.
- Named routes or typed helpers; no scattered raw route strings.
- Protect routes via guards using session and entitlements ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Build navigation trees from union(role/module/user grants) ∩ subscription package ∩ assigned modules ∩ ABAC scope. Omit unauthorized destinations from shell, drawer, rail, and menu bar.
- Deep links to unauthorized routes must redirect to localized forbidden/not-found states ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Stable readable web URLs using `human_friendly_id` where resource IDs appear; deep-link support where required.
- No navigation in repositories or data sources.
- Localized not-found page for unknown routes.
- Responsive shell for persistent navigation ([`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc)).

## Shell rules

- Shell route for persistent navigation.
- Mobile: bottom nav or drawer by destination count.
- Tablet: rail or compact side nav.
- Desktop/web: menu bar and side nav with collapse support.
- No duplicate pages for mobile/desktop unless interaction truly differs.

